        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 56.16,
          "end": 59.16,
          "en": "and you will always find improvement potential,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 59.16,
          "end": 63.07,
          "en": "but generally what we have here shouldn't be too bad.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 63.07,
          "end": 67.93,
          "en": "We are, for example, already using Nextimage.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 67.93,
          "end": 71.4,
          "en": "So the optimized images in all the places",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 71.4,
          "end": 73.61,
          "en": "where we are working with images,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 73.61,
          "end": 75.69,
          "en": "even in our post contents.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 75.69,
          "end": 79.11,
          "en": "Even there we make sure that images",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 79.11,
          "end": 83.77,
          "en": "that are part of our posts are rendered with Nextimage.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 83.77,
          "end": 86.3,
          "en": "And that is a great optimization",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 86.3,
          "end": 89.73,
          "en": "because that loads images only when they are needed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 89.73,
          "end": 94.38,
          "en": "It loads them lazily, and it also shrinks them in size.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 94.38,
          "end": 96.25,
          "en": "Now, speaking of lazy loading,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 96.25,
          "end": 101.25,
          "en": "that also is a concept we know in general in React,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 101.46000000000001,
          "end": 105.32,
          "en": "and most prominently when working with just React,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 105.32,
          "end": 109.81,
          "en": "without NextJS, you might want to lazy load your routes.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 109.81,
          "end": 112.61,
          "en": "So that the code for a given page",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 112.61,
          "end": 116.62,
          "en": "is only downloaded if you're visiting that page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 116.62,
          "end": 120.17,
          "en": "and it's not downloaded if you not visit the page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 120.17,
          "end": 123.21,
          "en": "The great thing here is that NextJS",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 123.21,
          "end": 126.24,
          "en": "has this kind of lazy loading built in.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 126.24,
          "end": 128.33,
          "en": "You don't need to worry about it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 128.33,
          "end": 131.56,
          "en": "Your different pages, which we have here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 131.56,
          "end": 133.33,
          "en": "are already lazy loaded.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 133.33,
          "end": 136.61,
          "en": "So the code for them is only fetched on demand,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 136.61,
          "end": 138.41,
          "en": "when we visit a page.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 138.41,
          "end": 140.54,
          "en": "So that built-in lazy loading",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 140.54,
          "end": 143,
          "en": "is a very nice feature to have.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 143,
          "end": 145.74,
          "en": "Now regarding the metadata, which we should add.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
